{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 42}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   TLS session tickets enable stateless connection resumption for\n   clients without server-side per-client state.  Servers vend session\n   tickets to clients, at their discretion, upon connection\n   establishment.  Clients store and use tickets when resuming future\n   connections.  Moreover, clients should use tickets at most once for\n   session resumption, especially if such keying material protects early\n   application data.  Single-use tickets bound the number of parallel\n   connections a client may initiate by the number of tickets received\n   from a given server.  To address this limitation, this document\n   describes a mechanism by which clients may specify the desired number\n   of tickets needed for future connections.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests/", "expires": "2019-07-22T23:32:31Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 233975, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/233975/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-01-19T00:33:19Z", "title": "TLS Ticket Requests", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   TLS session tickets enable stateless connection resumption for\n   clients without server-side per-client state.  Servers vend session\n   tickets to clients, at their discretion, upon connection\n   establishment.  Clients store and use tickets when resuming future\n   connections.  Moreover, clients should use tickets at most once for\n   session resumption, especially if such keying material protects early\n   application data.  Single-use tickets bound the number of parallel\n   connections a client may initiate by the number of tickets received\n   from a given server.  To address this limitation, this document\n   describes a mechanism by which clients may specify the desired number\n   of tickets needed for future connections.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests/", "expires": "2019-07-22T23:32:31Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 233974, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/233974/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-01-19T00:32:31Z", "title": "TLS Ticket Requests", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   TLS session tickets enable stateless connection resumption for\n   clients without server-side, per-client state.  Servers vend an\n   arbitrary number of session tickets to clients, at their discretion,\n   upon connection establishment.  Clients store and use tickets when\n   resuming future connections.  This document describes a mechanism by\n   which clients may specify the desired number of tickets needed for\n   future connections.  This extension aims to provide a means for\n   servers to determine the number of tickets to generate in order to\n   reduce ticket waste, while simultaneously priming clients for future\n   connection attempts.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests/", "expires": "2019-12-09T00:47:24Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 242396, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/242396/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-06-06T23:47:24Z", "title": "TLS Ticket Requests", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   TLS session tickets enable stateless connection resumption for\n   clients without server-side, per-client state.  Servers vend an\n   arbitrary number of session tickets to clients, at their discretion,\n   upon connection establishment.  Clients store and use tickets when\n   resuming future connections.  This document describes a mechanism by\n   which clients may specify the desired number of tickets needed for\n   future connections.  This extension aims to provide a means for\n   servers to determine the number of tickets to generate in order to\n   reduce ticket waste, while simultaneously priming clients for future\n   connection attempts.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests/", "expires": "2020-03-30T23:47:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 249970, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/249970/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-09-27T23:47:14Z", "title": "TLS Ticket Requests", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   TLS session tickets enable stateless connection resumption for\n   clients without server-side, per-client state.  Servers vend an\n  