ckets enable stateless connection resumption for\n   clients without server-side, per-client, state.  Servers vend an\n   arbitrary number of session tickets to clients, at their discretion,\n   upon connection establishment.  Clients store and use tickets when\n   resuming future connections.  This document describes a mechanism by\n   which clients can specify the desired number of tickets needed for\n   future connections.  This extension aims to provide a means for\n   servers to determine the number of tickets to generate in order to\n   reduce ticket waste, while simultaneously priming clients for future\n   connection attempts.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests/", "expires": "2021-06-07T02:20:22Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 291749, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/291749/", "rev": "07", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/154/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/25/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/"], "time": "2021-08-09T22:28:39Z", "title": "TLS Ticket Requests", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   TLS session tickets enable stateless connection resumption for\n   clients without server-side, per-client, state.  Servers vend an\n   arbitrary number of session tickets to clients, at their discretion,\n   upon connection establishment.  Clients store and use tickets when\n   resuming future connections.  This document describes a mechanism by\n   which clients can specify the desired number of tickets needed for\n   future connections.  This extension aims to provide a means for\n   servers to determine the number of tickets to generate in order to\n   reduce ticket waste, while simultaneously priming clients for future\n   connection attempts.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests/", "expires": "2021-06-07T02:20:22Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 291817, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/291817/", "rev": "07", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/154/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/116/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/"], "time": "2021-08-11T03:59:32Z", "title": "TLS Ticket Requests", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}]}